    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0649" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/5840: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panamá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-26T16:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>213. Reference Department’s No. 164, March 19, 2 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >midnight</hi>.] I discussed this question with the Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="77" xml:id="d582-f1"/> on March 23. He has today informed
                    me that the Cabinet has considered it and referred it to the Banco Agropecuario
                    for examination and recommendation as to price. The Minister said that the
                    Government had already offered certain local rubber producers a price higher
                    than that proposed by the United States. He will advise me further as soon as
                    the report is received from the bank.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d582-f1" n="77" xml:id="d582-f1-content">
